# Copy to .env and replace vault/item/field names with real 1Password references.
# Then run any tool through: ./run_with_1password.sh <command...>
#
# IMPORTANT: devx-cli's own ServiceNow auth (`devx-cli auth --add`) is
# browser-based OAuth per-person — it has no username/password/env-var
# injection surface, so it CANNOT be wrapped through 1Password or this
# .env file. Each person who runs this repo's tools authenticates their
# own devx-cli session once via `devx-cli auth --add`, same as today.
#
# This file is for any OTHER credential a future tool in this repo needs
# (e.g. a webhook token, an API key for a non-devx-cli integration). There
# are none required as of 2026-10-02 — this file intentionally has no
# real entries yet. When a tool does need one, add it here as an op://
# reference (mirroring Enterprise_RTB/.env.1password.example), never as a
# literal value, and never commit the resolved .env itself.
#
# Example shape, once something is actually needed:
# SOME_API_TOKEN="op://Vault Name/Item Name/field"
